{:edb/db-before-t 1184 :edb/db-after-t 1185 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534497 50 #inst "2026-10-07T09:07:35.135Z" 13194139534497 true] [17592186064281 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291956 13194139534497 true] [17592186064282 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291932 13194139534497 true] [17592186064282 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291946 13194139534497 true] [17592186064283 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291939 13194139534497 true] [17592186064283 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291949 13194139534497 true] [17592186291932 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291933 13194139534497 true] [17592186291932 1089 "q-19302" 13194139534497 true] [17592186291932 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534497 true] [17592186291932 1100 "The position $s(t)$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)={t}^{2}-2t+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity at time $t=3.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." 13194139534497 true] [17592186291932 1113 #uuid "3df15b1d-5c6a-5a31-88c3-94f27234c33f" 13194139534497 true] [17592186291932 1145 "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2t+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\  & =2t-2+\\frac{1}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=3,$ we substitute $t=3$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =2(3)-2+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =6-2+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{3} \\\\  & =4.333\\,333… \\\\  & ≈4.33\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534497 true] [17592186291933 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291934 13194139534497 true] [17592186291933 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291935 13194139534497 true] [17592186291933 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291936 13194139534497 true] [17592186291933 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291937 13194139534497 true] [17592186291933 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291938 13194139534497 true] [17592186291933 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534497 true] [17592186291933 1041 "selection" 13194139534497 true] [17592186291933 1104 #e